SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn | Beyond the Basics: Elevating Engagement with Anthology Engage
DESCRIPTION:In today's rapidly evolving educational landscape\, fostering meaningful engagement is more crucial than ever. Anthology Engage provides institutions with a dynamic platform to streamline communication\, enhance collaboration\, and strengthen connections across campus communities. This presentation will explore key strategies for leveraging Anthology Engage to maximize student involvement\, improve institutional effectiveness\, and create a more cohesive digital environment. Attendees will gain insights into best practices\, innovative features\, and real-world applications that empower users to drive engagement and achieve institutional success. Whether you're new to Anthology or looking to optimize your current approach\, this session will equip you with the tools and knowledge needed to elevate engagement to new heights.
LOCATION:Falcon Center Conference Room 301
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/dd8d8d33-6b7e-4de7-ad60-cacb18fd6da297d3372d-25fe-4caf-ac45-ab03cb12f1cc.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:11416692@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173205Z
DTSTART:20251111T172000Z
DTEND:20251111T182000Z
SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn | Under Pressure: Government\, Higher Education\, and the Future of Civic Learning
DESCRIPTION:Presented by: Samantha Godbey This Lunch and Learn unpacks the increasingly politicized space that higher education occupies in U.S. public discourse and policymaking. From legislative action on curriculum content to challenges to public funding and student activism\, colleges are at the center of broader societal debates about free speech\, inclusion\, civic responsibility\, and the purpose of higher education itself.
LOCATION:Falcon Center Conference Room 301
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/992bb359-d7f9-43d3-8fdf-10b4d46c272a2d3d9824-4359-4ddf-995a-cd1d559aee85.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:11416694@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173205Z
DTSTART:20250916T162000Z
DTEND:20250916T172000Z
SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn | Paving the Path: Building Transformative Co-Curricular Journeys
DESCRIPTION:Presented by: Justin Rader In today's dynamic educational landscape\, co-curricular experiences play a pivotal role in shaping holistic student development. This session explores innovative approaches to designing meaningful co-curricular journeys that foster engagement\, leadership\, and personal growth. Through interactive discussions and practical insights\, we will uncover strategies to create programs that not only complement academic learning but also empower students to navigate their passions\, develop essential life skills\, and drive positive change. Whether you're an educator\, administrator\, or student affairs professional\, join us in discovering how to pave the way for impactful co-curricular experiences that leave a lasting imprint.
LOCATION:Falcon Center Conference Room 301
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/2b3fa1c6-d367-43bf-95c8-21c60fcb934150d64cd0-3835-49a6-ad1f-9c6ffc8ba82e.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:11416696@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173205Z
DTSTART:20250902T162000Z
DTEND:20250902T172000Z
SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn | Discovering the many colors of our West Virginia Birds
DESCRIPTION:Presented by: Joey Herron Birding in West Virginia is not only an exciting experience\, but a learning experience\, discovering the over 300 species that have been seen in West Virginia. Red \, yellow\, blue......what color is your favorite? Our birds will amaze you with a variety of colors that paint beautiful picture of our "flying resources".
LOCATION:Falcon Center Conference Room 301
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/d026fc48-2991-4936-8e0a-c268ece0bb8f4f12dde1-4619-48a8-bbc8-b7c4cabd4fe9.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:11416708@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173205Z
DTSTART:20250909T162000Z
DTEND:20250909T172000Z
SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn | AI for OER Discovery: Maximizing Course Design
DESCRIPTION:Presented by: Derek Nuzum Open Educational Resources (OER) serve educators and learners alike by providing high quality educational content for free. However\, locating relevant OER databases/materials\, navigating various database UI's\, and manually searching materials requires a serious time investment. Properly utilizing AI to locate OER allows us to expedite this process and maximize our time. Reclaim time for the important things (like collaborating with colleagues and meeting with students) by learning how to locate OER with AI!
LOCATION:Falcon Center Conference Room 301
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/b744a720-6a0e-41a0-8c1c-ec3e6903e222e461be7b-7c3e-4ed6-9620-403d02119309.png
END:VEVENT
