BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:11524669@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20250925T162000Z
DTEND:20250925T172000Z
SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn | AIMSS: Supporting Neurodivergent Students on Campus 
DESCRIPTION:Presented by: Cicely Jones The Autism Individualized Mentoring and Support Services (AIMSS) Program would like to raise awareness of Autism and other neurodivergent diagnoses. We would like to provide an overview of the services AIMSS offers to support students and ways in which faculty and staff can help support our efforts. In addition\, we would like to share response data from our recent surveys and information regarding new initiatives we have in development.
LOCATION:Falcon Center Private Dining
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/54e4b0dc-40f7-4489-8346-d3679f303af638f7b1ca-eecd-4030-8dcd-9257c9615d6f.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:11524682@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20251119T230000Z
DTEND:20251120T003000Z
SUMMARY:Echoes at Gettysburg: An Anniversary Analysis of Lincoln’s Address
DESCRIPTION:On the anniversary of Abraham Lincolns iconic Gettysburg Address\, join us for an engaging exploration of one of the most influential speeches in American history. Dr. Chris Bondi\, will guide us through a detailed analysis of the speechs structure\, language\, and enduring impact. From its historical context to its rhetorical brilliance\, this program will offer fresh insights into why Lincolns words continue to resonate more than 160 years later.
LOCATION:Falcon Center 301\, Falcon Center
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/1892306e-bfa0-498c-99b8-56ec6e6672626427ac2e-5c49-48e7-b1f7-7777482b0b94.png
END:VEVENT
