UID:11526885@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20251027T220000Z
DTEND:20251027T233000Z
SUMMARY: Monsters of the Mountain State: Fact or Folklore?
DESCRIPTION:From eerie shadows in the hills to glowing eyes in the night\, West Virginias legendary creatures have captured imaginations for generations. But are these monsters real\, or just spooky campfire stories passed down through the years? In this Halloween debate\, the Fairmont State Debate Team will face off over the truth behind the Mountain States most famous cryptids.You be the judge: fact or folklore? This event takes place both on Monday Oct 27 at 6pm and Tuesday Oct 28 at 12:30pm. Students\, staff\, and community members are invited!
LOCATION:Frank and Jane Gabor Folklife Center\, 1201 Locust Avenue\, Fairmont\, WV
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/332eee08-8306-409b-addf-2e83d7f542c9188bab82-2cdc-45e2-a0b0-9edcbfcd9135.png
END:VEVENT
