SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn | Collaborative Online International Learning VE & Study Abroad (Branded Programs vs Faculty Led Programs)
DESCRIPTION:Presented by: Rosemarie Igbo\, Dr. Barbara MacLennan\, and Dr. Maria Agee Join the Office of Global Engagement to learn more about Study Abroad and Virtual Exchange. Unfamiliar with the topic? No worries! Here's a little crash course: Branded Programs-faculty decide the best semester for their students to study abroad on the program and pre-approve a set of courses for students to take. This creates a clear pathway toward graduation that includes study abroad and aligns with the goals of the academic unit. Faculty Led Programs - Customized programs that meet a specific objective. A professor travels with a group of students and either teaches a course or oversees a project or internship. COIL VE - Virtual Exchange (VE) or Collaborative Online International Learning (COIL) is an innovative pedagogy that allows professors and students to use technology to engage with their peers at universities around the globe.
LOCATION:Falcon Center Conference Room 301
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/8d60fd4f-d685-4f22-9021-6c153a35af107e2629a1-3aea-4cd6-94e8-c9083c858910.png
END:VEVENT
