SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn | Computer Technology Mysteries Series
DESCRIPTION:Presented by: Gary Edwards Join us for an eye-opening journey that demystifies the technology you use every day. This isn't your typical tech workshopwe're going beyond tips and tricks to reveal the fascinating "mechanical" processes that make computers tick. What You'll Discover How computers actually "think" and process the data you create The surprisingly logical steps behind seemingly magical technology Why understanding these fundamentals can transform your relationship with technology Real-world insights that make everyday computer use less frustrating and more intuitive Perfect For You If : You've ever felt confused or intimidated by technology You're curious about what happens "behind the scenes" You want to understand the why behind computer behavior\, not just the how You're ready to see computers as the logical machines they really are What Makes This Series Special These presentations distill 47 years of IT expertise and 40 years of teaching experience into clear\, jargon-free explanations. We focus on core concepts that illuminate how computer technology actually worksno prior technical experience required. This is NOT a "tips and hints" session. You won't learn Excel shortcuts or Windows hacks. Instead\, you'll gain something more valuable: genuine understanding of the technology that surrounds us.
LOCATION:Library SkyLab
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/b6ee7db5-17af-4124-a5a7-3bce27df6cea5090fe20-e5b3-4510-a06e-84891f1b7219.png
END:VEVENT
