SUMMARY:Taking a Census Snapshot in Higher Education: Turning Data into Action
DESCRIPTION:Understanding who your students are at any given moment is critical for informed decision-making in higher education. This workshop introduces participants to the concept of a census snapshota fixed point in time when institutions capture official enrollment\, demographic\, and academic data for reporting\, planning\, and accreditation purposes. Participants will learn: Why census dates matter and how they connect to compliance\, funding\, and institutional accountability. Best practices for collecting\, validating\, and storing census data. Ways to translate a census snapshot into meaningful insights for student success\, resource allocation\, and policy development. Common challenges (e.g.\, late adds/drops\, data integrity issues) and strategies for ensuring accuracy. *Lunch will be provided to participants
LOCATION:Falcon Center Conference Rooms 301 and 302
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/9e1bf066-c77d-4410-8426-a49e1d1ac2922b4a2c23-b7da-43bf-8869-d0f7fa02d0ad.png
END:VEVENT
