UID:11986551@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20260116T010000Z
DTEND:20260116T020000Z
SUMMARY:Life After the Residence Hall with RA Kam
DESCRIPTION:Life After the Residence Hall prepares residents for the transition from on-campus housing to independent living. This session explores what it means to live on your own\, including managing finances\, understanding leases\, maintaining a household\, balancing responsibilities\, and using community resources. Through discussion and practical scenarios\, residents will reflect on their readiness for independent living and identify skills they need to strengthen. The program encourages forward-thinking\, responsibility\, and confidence as students plan for life beyond the residence hall.
LOCATION:UT Main Lounge
URL:https://static.campuslabsengage.com/discovery/images/events/social.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:11986566@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20260125T200000Z
DTEND:20260125T210000Z
SUMMARY:New Year Good Things Jar
DESCRIPTION:Join RA Quinn in making a New Years resolution jar! You'll get to decorate your jar with paint and discover a new skill to remember good things that happen every day\, week\, or month to look back on when you're having a hard day. Bring your own jar or use one of the mason jars provided! Paint will be provided and paintbrushes\, you may bring your own if you please!
LOCATION:2nd Floor Lobby BP
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/5849cd43-8631-452e-b5ed-5a44de706621456643d6-c79c-495d-aeae-27e977c34598.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:11986838@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20260421T162000Z
DTEND:20260421T172000Z
SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn: A day without laughter is day wasted? (Do we really need humor in lives?)
DESCRIPTION:Abstract: This presentation will examine the characteristics of humor and its role in peoples every day lives (in areas such as health psychology\, clinical psychology\, and positive psychology) Location: Falcon Center Conference Room 301 Date: April 21\, 2026 Time: 12:20-1:20
LOCATION:Falcon Center Conference Room 301
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/dcce996f-a3c6-45fc-8b2e-4eeb6f00a9a89f34afc4-7bea-4ef4-ba1e-f7a2b48057b2.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:11986844@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20260414T162000Z
DTEND:20260414T172000Z
SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn: Your Vote\, Your Voice: Student Engagement in Midterm Elections
DESCRIPTION:Abstract: This interactive discussion will focus on the role of students and young adults in midterm elections and highlight practical ways to engage civically. We will examine trends in youth voting\, discuss why participation matters even when presidential candidates are not on the ballot\, and provide tools for registration\, planning to vote\, and navigating state-specific rules. The session will emphasize how students choices can influence not only national policy but also state and local offices that directly affect campus communities and young adult priorities. There will be a specific conversation of how to vote via absentee ballot. Location: Falcon Center Conference Room 301 Date: April 14\, 2026 Time: 12:20-1:20
LOCATION:Falcon Center Conference Room 301
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/e492d86b-af93-4aad-ba38-7d3167e9652e11734881-d086-4419-8045-f47c01597880.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:11986848@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20260317T162000Z
DTEND:20260317T172000Z
SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn: Kicking & Punching: How Martial Arts Helped Me Develop Discipline
DESCRIPTION:Abstract: This presentation will share Isabella's experience studying kenpo ju jutsu\, a form of martial arts that focuses on practical self-defense. Attendees can expect to learn general principles of the art\, elements of self-defense\, and how martial arts could benefit them. Location: Falcon Center Conference Room 301 Date: March 17\, 2026 Time: 12:20-1:20
LOCATION:Falcon Center Conference Room 301
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/327457ac-4359-4a43-8319-26efbeb5a617c1db1170-1563-4f5b-9a91-1938d10f8955.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:11986853@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20260303T172000Z
DTEND:20260303T182000Z
SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn: Midterms Matter: Understanding How Elections Shape Our World
DESCRIPTION:Abstract: This session will explore what midterm elections are\, why they are a crucial part of the democratic process\, and how they affect policies that influence everyday lifefrom education and healthcare to state and local governance. Participants will learn how midterms determine control of Congress and other elected offices\, why voter turnout tends to be lower than in presidential years\, and how young voters can make a meaningful impact through participation. By the end of the session\, students will have a clearer picture of how midterm elections work and why their voices matter in shaping public policy and community outcomes. Location: Falcon Center Conference Room 301 Date: March 3\, 2026 Time: 12:20-1:20
LOCATION:Falcon Center Conference Room 301
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/559c5068-d8cb-4470-885b-f973f8a36a764b1bbd37-a3cf-4303-8dd5-db165779a2ff.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:11986874@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20260217T172000Z
DTEND:20260217T182000Z
SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn: Tales We Tell: Storytelling at Fairmont State
DESCRIPTION:Abstract: In this presentation\, Journalism Professor Laura Harbert\, PhD. and Folklife Center Director Lydia Warren\, PhD.share the ways stories are communicated on campus through storytelling events\, journalism\, and archives.They will share their vision for increasing the accessibility of storytelling at Fairmont State University for students\, staff\, faculty\, and the larger community. Location: Falcon Center Conference Room 301 Date: February 17\, 2026 Time: 12:20-1:20
LOCATION:Falcon Center Conference Room 301
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/d0a58599-d5d6-4af2-94a6-44814b19e0e0aa7928f8-86e8-452f-b9ba-a4e4c7523c32.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:11986886@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20260210T172000Z
DTEND:20260210T182000Z
SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn: A Practical Guide to Navigating Intellectual Property in the Classroom
DESCRIPTION:Abstract: During this session\, we will discuss some "Best Practices" for use of Intellectual Property in the Classroom. From understanding the Fair Use exception\, to using items in the public domain\, and Creative Commons licenses. This session should provide helpful guidance\, resources and advice so you can confidently share protected materials in both your in-person\, hybrid\, and online classes. Location: Falcon Center Conference Room 301 Date: February 10\, 2026 Time: 12:20-1:20
LOCATION:Falcon Center Conference Room 301
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/21aa367a-4145-4483-845c-2cdfe6000dda1fffb0f6-0e87-4fb2-a7a4-e65c4908ab1a.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:11986892@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20260203T172000Z
DTEND:20260203T182000Z
SUMMARY:Lunch and Learn: Identifying & Addressing Generative AI Assignment Submissions
DESCRIPTION:Abstract: Are you contemplating the level of involvement of generative AI tools like ChatGPT have had in completing assignments for your courses? Have you tried everything from AI text detection softwares to forensic investigation with disappointing results? This session equips faculty with practical\, discipline-agnostic methods for recognizing generative AI assisted assignment submissions. Well cover common indicators of generative AI text\, why generative AI text detection tools are less helpful than you think\, and constructive responses to your students that will promote academic integrity. Youll leave with sample syllabus statements\, a framework for responding to suspected generative AI use\, and ideas that will prompt students to critically evaluate the role of generative AI in their learning. Location: Falcon Center Conference Room 301 Date: February 3\, 2026 Time: 12:20-1:20
LOCATION:Falcon Center Conference Room 301
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/7b6ae4ed-8d2a-4f02-816d-cb52e5b3ec5f06512fa5-c9c4-4162-9f9a-a38a970702d3.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:11986897@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20260120T172000Z
