SUMMARY:Work\, Rights\, and Power: A Public Debate on Labor Policy
DESCRIPTION:Hosted by the Fairmont State University Debate Team\, this public debate examines contemporary labor rights issues\, including worker protections\, collective bargaining\, wages\, and the role of government in the workplace. The event features a structured\, evidence-based format that models civil discourse and invites community engagement on the future of work and workers rights.
LOCATION:Folklife Center\, Folklife Center\, Fairmont \, WV
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/8f2c2d7b-84a3-4df4-98de-1ec977069d451a5d5282-d2b9-4aea-af3f-8fe4d638dd8a.png
