SUMMARY:Almost Maine Auditions 
DESCRIPTION:Almost Maine Auditions- Open to all current Fairmont State University students- undergraduates and graduate https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1mvC37fdLRdLlZWuNq6zSAOMgQx1m2InX?usp=sharing The dates are listed and will consist of two parts: 1.) A reading of 2 of the monologues found in the audition packet. Note they DO NOT need to be memorized but should have clear and distinct character choices. Remember\, this is a comedy! 2.) Cold reading during each of the 2 auditions times. Those parts will be added to the audition packet before auditions begin. Helpful hints: each character is a completely different person. Change your delivery as much as you can for each character you audition for. Pay attention to the descriptions given. I hope to cast at least 8-10 people but can cast more. The more people that I am able to cast\, the easier rehearsals will be. The entire play is posted\, please read it if you have time. Lastly\, please do not be overly concerned about the intimacy in some of the pieces. Each one will be tailored to your comfort and the needs of the story. You will be able to express your comfort level with intimacy on your audition information sheet. No one will be required to do anything that makes them uncomfortable. If you have questions or can't access the Google drive\, please let Troy Snyder know. His email is Troy.Snyder@fairmontstate.edu
LOCATION:314 Wallman Hall\, 1201 Locust Ave.\, Fairmont\, WV
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/de06eb41-121f-4060-879e-be23f54603d3483331c7-ecd1-4fce-8897-6b78bd8566f4.png
END:VEVENT
