SUMMARY:VEX Robotics - Call for Volunteers! 
DESCRIPTION:As most of you know\, the SciTech Education Resource Center manages a wide range of competitive STEM programs\, but none are bigger than the VEX Robotics State Championship series.. and WE REALLY NEED VOLUNTEERS! ROBOTS IN THE FALCON CENTER! Calling all students\, faculty and staff. We Need YOU to volunteer at the annual VEX Robotics State Championship series of tournaments that are held at the Falcon Center over Spring Break. If you arent leaving town\, consider helping inspire the next generation of Falcons by judging or score keeping for one of the upcoming tournaments. If you can commit one day\,please sign up for ourMiddle School V5 Championship onTuesday March 10OR theMiddle School VEX IQ Championship on Thursday\, March 12. If you can give two days\,we humbly request you volunteer for theHigh School V5 Championship on Sunday\, March 8 Monday\, March 9or theElementary VEX IQ Championship on Friday March 13 Saturday\, March 14. If you only have a few hoursand want a free CrossFit workout\, wed love your help loading\, unloading\, and setting up/breaking down the tournaments onSaturday 3/6\, Wednesday 3/11\, and/or Sunday 3/15. The success of these events\, and our future enrollment\, is in your hands Sign up using the link below. The highest-need roles are judging and scorekeeping.No prior experience is requiredfor any role. https://www.signupgenius.com/go/10C0D44AEAF2CA4FBC43-58024665-2026#/
LOCATION:Falcon Center
