SUMMARY:Here’s a Little Sucker for a Sweet Day! with RA Alicia
DESCRIPTION:is a passive stress-relief program designed to provide residents with a small but meaningful boost during busy or high-stress times in the semester. A table or bulletin board will be set up in the residence hall lobby with a bowl of assorted lollipops and a short encouraging message reminding students to take a moment for themselves. Residents are invited to grab a lollipop as a sweet treat and reflect on one positive thing they have accomplished recently. This simple grab-and-go activity promotes resilience\, self-reflection\, and community care while creating a lighthearted and supportive atmosphere within the hall. Participation will be measured by the number of lollipops taken and any optional encouragement notes left by residents.
