SUMMARY:Small Bears\, Big Impact
DESCRIPTION:RISE invites Fairmont State students\, staff and faculty to participate in Small Bears\, Big Impact: A Community Bear Hug for Kids in Care! In honor of Child Abuse Prevention Month in April and Foster Care Awareness Month in May\, the student organization is hosting a community- and University-wide collection of teddy bears to be donated and distributed in partnership with West Virginia CASA\, a statewide child advocacy network. RISE has a goal to collect 6\,000 bears enough for each child currently in the child welfare system in West Virginia. All you have to do is bring in a teddy bear no taller than 12-inches to Prichard Hall during collection days and times (Monday\, April 6th to Friday\, April 10th\, 8:00am-4:00pm).
LOCATION:115 Prichard Hall
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/67d60a0b-3122-489e-afec-800e8c9ddbf33412301a-015c-4e55-97d1-e1401be0f591.png
