SUMMARY:American Association of Geographers 2026 Watch Party & National Geography Conference
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an AAG Node Watch Party\, where we stream live sessions from the American As sociation of Geographers Annual Meeting in San Francisco to right here on campus. This is a free opportunity (normally $300 +per person) to explore careers and hear from experts across fields including: Geography and GIS Digital Humanities Cultural Geography and History\, AI and data science Public health Psychology Environmental science Urban planning Disaster response Business and logistics Sustainability Education Government and policy and more. . . Participation counts as attending the conference for professional development and resume building. Drop in to the GISS Lab in 308 Hardway Hall before sessions for San Francisco themed snacks\, games\, and prizes. To check out the schedule of events please use the Program Link.
LOCATION:GISS Lab in 308 Hardway Hall
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/b3bb69fa-9b41-409e-926a-91de9b8611620a69ecf0-0941-40d4-ac93-3d0cd31145a9.png
