DTSTART:20260331T190000Z
DTEND:20260331T200000Z
SUMMARY:Falcon Success Lounge
DESCRIPTION:Tired of Playing the Background Character in Your Own Life? Weve all been there: staring at a confusing syllabus\, doing 90% of a group project alone\, or watching a perfect internship opportunity slide by because you didn't want to "be a bother." If you dont find your voice\, you stay exactly where you are. Thats the reality of "Speak Up or Stay Stuck." Self-advocacy sounds like corporate-speak\, but its actually a survival skill. This workshop is a low-pressure\, high-vibe space designed to help you stop overthinking and start asking for what you actually need. Whats in it for you? The "Group Project" Fix: Learn how to set boundaries without being the "mean" one. Professor Communication: Master the art of the "ask" (extensions\, clarity\, or references) without the panic attack. The Confidence Shift: Go from "I guess this is fine" to "Actually\, heres what I need to succeed." Zero Cringe: No forced role-playing or "trust falls." Just real talk\, actual strategies\, and probably some decent snacks. The Vibe: Casual. The Goal: Getting you unstuck. The Energy: Main Character. Don't let your goals get sidelined because you were too polite to claim them. Come hang out\, vent a little\, and leave with the tools to speak up for yourself.
LOCATION:Ruth Ann Musick Library- 2nd Floor\, 1201 Locust Ave\, Fairmont\, WV
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/478d7654-afb0-40d9-a3e9-5c47645ccd7f2581f13e-a361-467c-919f-927f97a0cdb0.png
END:VEVENT
