DTEND:20260421T172000Z
SUMMARY:Crafting and Compost- Plan(t)ing a World Without Waste
DESCRIPTION:Join us in the Botany Lab (HHH 402) to learn about how to transform food waste into garden abundance through composting. We'll learn about the compost process then you can plant a native wildflower or herb seedling. Envision a world without trash as we recycle materials to make and decorate a pot for your new seedling friend to go home with you. This event is part of our Zero Trash Utopia series\, so we look forward to announcing the winner of our trash identification competition\, too! However\, no need to have attended the prior event to come plant with us here!
LOCATION:Hunt Haught Hall 402- the Botany Lab\, Hunt Haught Hall\, Fairmont\, WV
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/0aa6bd05-b9d5-41dc-8e2a-2817d64713871e8690b9-d267-4e4f-b6af-6e4c2fc33245.png
