SUMMARY:Come Weave A Tale Youth Storytelling Day-Camp
DESCRIPTION:Come Weave A Tale Youth Storytelling Day-Camp hosted by the WV Storytelling Guild and Fairmont State University. Drop off - 7:30 a.m. to 7:55 a.m. Camp begins at 8 a.m. and ends at 5 p.m. Pick up - 5:00 p.m. to 5:30 p.m. Who: Students in grades 6 through 12 Tuition - $200\; $175 for those who register before May 1. Fifty-percent scholarships are available for those who qualify. What to expect:Experience active\, fun\, and informative instruction in traditional story preparation and performance\, plus creative add-ons like puppetry and theatre games from professional storytellers and Fairmont State instructors. Appreciate a tour of the beautiful Fairmont State University campus. Spend time in the Ruth Ann Musick Library. Enjoy the Falcon Center pool\; lunch in the Fairmont State dining hall\; free snacks. Get a behindthescenes look at a dress rehearsal of the Town & Gown production of the hit musical Come From Away. Perform a story on Thursday evening for family and friends. Have fun and make new friends! For registration and scholarship information\, contact Francene Kirk: francene.kirk@fairmontstate.edu or francene.kirk@gmail.com
LOCATION:The Frank and Jane Gabor West Virginia Folklife Center\, 1201 Locust Ave.\, Fairmont\, WV
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/9728f9b9-0a89-47bd-af89-c6b938cb6134ec995e52-a6af-475a-98f0-281dfa029aef.png
END:VEVENT
