BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:12449967@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20260529T210000Z
DTEND:20260530T000000Z
SUMMARY:Intro to Kayaking
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to explore the basics of paddling with our Intro to Kayaking Workshop at the Falcon Center on May 29th! This beginner-friendly program is perfect for anyone interested in learning the fundamentals of kayaking in a safe\, supportive environmentno prior experience needed. The workshop will be divided into two engaging segments: land-based instruction and in-water practice. During the land portion\, participants will be introduced to the essential components of a kayak and paddle\, proper equipment use\, safety guidelines\, and basic paddling techniques. Once comfortable with the fundamentals\, participants will transition to the water for hands-on experience\, where theyll practice skills such as entering and exiting the kayak\, basic strokes\, and maneuvering. Participants should come prepared to get wet and are encouraged to wear comfortable\, water-appropriate clothing. Participants are also encouraged to bring their own kayak\, as limited supply will be available for those without.
LOCATION:Falcon Center - Gym 1/Pool\, 1201 Locust Ave Falcon Center - Gym 1/Pool\, Fairmont\, West Virginia
URL:https://static.campuslabsengage.com/discovery/images/events/learning.jpg
END:VEVENT
