BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:12485871@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20260731T120000Z
DTEND:20260801T220000Z
SUMMARY:Volunteer Opportunity: West Virginia Robotics Extreme (WVRoX) – 2-day endurance robotics competition
DESCRIPTION:Fairmont State University's SciTech Education Resource Center\, in coordination with Mountaineer Area RoboticS FIRST Robotics Competition (FRC) team 2614\, is hosting the semi-annual WVRoX endurance robotics competition. This one-of-a-kind event features 30 FRC teams from across the nation competing through the night in a test of ingenuity and endurance. As you can imagine\, a large number of volunteers are needed to make this event happen. Volunteers serve in 4-hour shifts in a variety of roles\, including roles for which no prior experience in robotics is necessary. More information about WVRoX\, including a volunteer signup link\, is available athttps://www.marsfirst.org/wvrox.
LOCATION:Fairmont State University Falcon Center
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/030c7daa-9dc4-432a-9ccb-6d9b145ba30741b00ae5-3c52-432e-8676-278d5c34d9ab.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:12485874@fairmontstate.edu
DTSTAMP:20260803T173206Z
DTSTART:20260916T220000Z
DTEND:20260916T233000Z
SUMMARY:Your Community\, Your Voice: Getting Engaged Where It Matters
DESCRIPTION:What does it actually mean to be an active member of your community and where do you start? Join Dani Devito\, President of the Marion County Chamber of Commerce\, for a candid conversation about civic participation\, local leadership\, and the tangible ways individuals can make a difference right here in Fairmont and North Central West Virginia. Drawing on years of experience working at the intersection of business\, government\, and community\, she will offer practical insight into how students and residents alike can find their civic voice\, plug into existing networks\, and help shape the future of the place they call home. Whether you are new to civic engagement or looking to deepen your involvement\, this talk is your invitation to show up.This event is part of Fairmont State University's Constitution Week programming\, a campuswide celebration of civic life\, democratic values\, and the enduring relevance of our founding documents.
LOCATION:Falcon Center 301\, 1201 Locust Avenue\, Fairmont\, WV
URL:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/7a0b61a0-23c7-49d5-9b27-cec8ca50ee9ad0509822-01e2-49e2-a26b-852a756ae319.png
END:VEVENT
